  "limitations": [
    "Operator create/rename/archive audits belong to the new operator and cannot be read through the current tenant-fenced audit API. Exact three-event audit/replay proof is automated-only; staging verifies native UI and canonical operator reads.",
    "Only fresh labelled operator, branch and unused future holiday fixtures are changed. The archived branch and its existing owned mirror are retained, never directly deleted.",
    "The fresh session switches to the fixture and back. GET /me exposes no station ID; no station selection or other session mutation is performed.",
    "Active equipment archive refusals, permission negatives, sold-holiday locks and uncertain readback cases are automated proof; no live equipment or payment record is changed.",
    "Unrelated operator/branch rows, navigation labels and signed-in person details are hidden for proof privacy; the asserted native controls and fixture records remain visible.",
    "Browser error kinds and partial attempts are retained. Passing these stated controls does not claim an error-free browser.",
    "Original local release/proof preparation remains54. Executed V2 is bound separately through the explicit amendment and actual14/83 rerun. Candidate-CSS geometry is inherited under identical capture code; font substitution and closed-dialog stubs remain disclosed.",
    "This validator checks retained public flags/fingerprints and the reviewed helper, without a new remote read. Exact preferences/estate equality, audit actor and session direction were checked inside that helper; the public receipt does not include those raw snapshots.",
    "No station-null state or live operator-audit proof is claimed. Operator audit/replay and permission/equipment/payment negatives remain automated-only.",
    "All3 images were viewed by the coordinator under the explicit command flag. The validator verifies PNG bytes/dimensions/bounds metadata, without inventing an independent pixel review.",
    "Browser error kinds are retained exactly and remain unclassified; passing the seven stated controls does not establish their cause or claim an error-free browser."
